course: dictionary
lesson: 381
title: Anyway: even so, or moving on
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Anyway is a small word with three main jobs. First, it means even so, in spite of something: «It was raining, but we went anyway.» The rain did not stop them, so anyway shows they went even though it was wet.
explain: Second, anyway moves a talk on or comes back to the main point: «Anyway, what did you do today?» Here the word signals that you are changing the subject. Third, it can mean in any case, whatever happens, as in «thanks anyway».
explain: Stories use anyway when a character does something despite a problem or a warning. Use the context to decide if the choice is brave or foolish: «being brave means doing the scary thing anyway, not feeling no fear.»
fact: Anyway means even so, in spite of something.
fact: Anyway can change the subject or bring a talk back to its main point.
fact: «Thanks anyway» means thank you even though the other person could not help.
fact: «Zara thanked her uncle anyway» even though the game was one she does not even play, so she was thankful for the gesture.
fact: In stories, anyway often shows a character going ahead despite a problem or warning, which can be brave or foolish.
exercise: «It was raining, but we went anyway.» What does anyway mean here? | *Even so, in spite of the rain | Quickly, before the rain started | Because of the rain | Under an umbrella
exercise: «Anyway, what did you do today?» What is anyway doing in this sentence? | *It changes the subject to a new question | It says sorry for something | It asks the listener to be quiet | It means very hungry
exercise: Zara felt a little disappointed but «thanked her uncle anyway». What does anyway show? | She said thank you very loudly | *She said thank you even though the gift was not one she could use | She said thank you because the gift was perfect | She refused to say thank you
test: Jayden says «thanks anyway» to a friend who could not help him. What does he mean? | Sorry for being late | *Thank you, even though you could not help | Goodbye for now | Thank you, because you helped a lot
test: In a story, a girl climbs the wobbly tree «anyway», even though her dad warned her. What does anyway show? | She climbs it slowly and quietly | She climbs because the warning made her feel safe | *She goes ahead despite the warning | She forgets the tree is there
exam: Which sentence uses anyway to change the subject? | *«Anyway, shall we go to the park?» | «It was cold, but she swam anyway.» | «We went to the park anyway, even though it rained.» | «Thanks anyway for trying to help.»
